gram","target":"https://www.lcsc.edu/news/2024/10/16/lc-state-prison-ed-program-receives-federal-approval-leads-the-way-in-idaho","line":58},{"title":"in a January 2023 study","target":"https://www.mackinac.org/S2023-01","line":84},{"title":"in an August 2019 study","target":"https://www.rand.org/content/dam/rand/pubs/perspectives/PE300/PE342/RAND_PE342.pdf","line":86}],"metadata":{"title":"‘Your circumstances do not define your ceiling:’ LC State prison program grows","source":"https://www.idahoednews.org/top-news/your-circumstances-do-not-define-your-ceiling-lc-state-prison-program-grows/","author":["[[Kevin Richert]]"],"published":"2026-05-25","created":"2026-07-08","description":"This year, 228 prison inmates enrolled in Lewis-Clark State College courses — up from 40 just three years ago. Federal support has helped fuel the program."},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},